{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_10a",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "The primary outcomes in this study were rates of PTB and stillbirth. Secondary outcomes included mean birthweight (continuous) and rates of low birthweight (LBW), spontaneous PTB, medically indicated PTB, and neonatal, perinatal, or maternal mortality. ... Outcomes were defined as follows: Preterm birth: Live births between 22 + 0 and 36 + 6 weeks of gestation were classified as PTB. ... Stillbirth: Death before the complete expulsion or extraction from the parturient of a product of human conception at or after 20 weeks of gestation. ... Birthweight: Infant weight in grams, measured as soon as possible after live birth. Birthweight < 2500 g was defined as LBW, birthweight < 1500 g was defined as very low birthweight (VLBW), and birthweight < 1000 gram was defined as extremely low birthweight (ELBW). Spontaneous PTB: Birth of a baby between 22 + 0 and 36 + 6 weeks of gestation following spontaneous preterm labor or preterm prelabor rupture of membranes. Medically indicated PTB: Preterm birth initiated by a healthcare provider for maternal or fetal indications. Neonatal mortality: Death of a newborn due to any cause before 28 days of age. Maternal mortality: Death of a woman either during pregnancy or childbirth from any cause related to or aggravated by pregnancy or its management, or within 42 days of end of pregnancy, irrespective of the duration and site of the pregnancy.",
      "reason": "The manuscript lists primary and secondary outcome domains and provides explicit definitions for each outcome domain (PTB, stillbirth, birthweight categories, spontaneous/medically indicated PTB, neonatal and maternal mortality)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "Preterm birth: Live births between 22 + 0 and 36 + 6 weeks of gestation were classified as PTB. Data on PTB at < 28 weeks, < 32 weeks, and < 34 weeks of gestation were reported separately in some studies and were analyzed independently. ... Stillbirth: Death before the complete expulsion or extraction from the parturient of a product of human conception at or after 20 weeks of gestation. ... Neonatal mortality: Death of a newborn due to any cause before 28 days of age. Maternal mortality: Death of a woman either during pregnancy or childbirth from any cause related to or aggravated by pregnancy or its management, or within 42 days of end of pregnancy.",
      "reason": "Time frames/measurement windows are specified for the outcome domains (gestational age ranges for PTB and stillbirth, neonatal mortality <28 days, maternal mortality within 42 days), and some specific gestational cut-offs are noted."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "Data on PTB at < 28 weeks, < 32 weeks, and < 34 weeks of gestation were reported separately in some studies and were analyzed independently. ... We contacted authors to obtain data on stillbirth and neonatal mortality when the outcomes were reported as 'intrauterine fetal death' and 'perinatal mortality'.",
      "reason": "The authors state that they analyzed different PTB cut-offs separately and that they contacted authors to obtain comparable outcome data in some cases, indicating efforts to capture compatible results; however, there is no explicit statement that all compatible results (all measures, time points, analyses) were sought for each outcome domain or a comprehensive description of scope, so the reporting is partial."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "For one study conducted in the Netherlands by Been et al, 54 data were presented using multiple cut-­ offs to define the pre-­ and post-­ pandemic periods, with several different comparisons, making it difficult to select one comparison that aligned well with the other studies; we, therefore, included this study in the systematic review but not in meta-­ analyses.",
      "reason": "The manuscript provides at least one example describing why a study was excluded from meta-analyses because multiple, non-aligning comparisons complicated selection, with an explicit rationale. However, there is no overarching, systematic description of the process used to select among multiple compatible results across all studies, so reporting is partial."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e5",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "The outcomes of intrauterine fetal death and perinatal mortality, though specified in the protocol, were not included ultimately in the review (deviation from protocol).",
      "reason": "The authors report a change from the protocol (certain protocol-specified outcomes were not ultimately included), which addresses a change in outcome-domain inclusion; however, the manuscript notes the deviation without providing a detailed rationale for why these specified outcomes were not included, so reporting is partial."
    },
